\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Saviour, quicken many nations,
\par Fruitful let Thy sorrows be;
\par By Thy pains and consolations 
\par Draw the Gentiles unto Thee:
\par Of Thy cross the wondrous story
\par Be to all the nations told;
\par Let them see Thee in Thy glory
\par And Thy mercy manifold.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Far and wide, thou all unknowig,
\par Pants for Thee each mortal breast;
\par Human tears for Thee are flowing,
\par Human hearts in Thee would rest;
\par Thirsting, as for dews of even,
\par As the new-mown grass for rain,
\par Thee they seek as God of heaven,
\par Thee as Man for sinners slain.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Saviour. lo! the isles are waiting,
\par Stretched the band and strained the sight,
\par For Thy Spirit, new creating, 
\par Love's pure flame, and wisdom's light;
\par Give the word, and of the preacher
\par Speed the foot, and touch the tongue;
\par Till on earth by every creature
\par Glory to the Lamb be sung.
\par Amen.
\par 
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

